// Rule name:      Account added to local Administrators group
// Detects:        A member was added to a security-enabled local group (Event ID 4732)
//                 where the group is BUILTIN\Administrators. Persistence or privilege escalation.
// Data source:    SecurityEvent via Windows Security Events (AMA)
// MITRE ATT&CK:   Persistence, Privilege Escalation / T1098.007 Account Manipulation: Additional Local or Domain Groups
// Severity:       High
// Schedule:       runs every 5 min, looks back 10 min (lookback > frequency for late AMA events)
// Threshold:      generate alert when results > 0
// Entity mapping: Account (Sid) = MemberSid, Host (FullName) = Computer; SubjectAccount = who made the change
// Tested:         not yet - planned trigger: local account created and added to Administrators via Azure Run Command
// Tuning notes:   Group matched by SID S-1-5-32-544, so it works on any OS language ("Administradores" on pt-BR).
//                 MemberName is "-" for local accounts; MemberSid is the reliable field.
//                 Lookback 10 min on a 5 min schedule can raise the same event twice; incident grouping by entities absorbs it.
//                 In production, exclude approved provisioning accounts.

SecurityEvent
| where TimeGenerated > ago(10m)
| where EventID == 4732
| where TargetSid == "S-1-5-32-544"   // BUILTIN\Administrators, any OS language
| project TimeGenerated, Computer, SubjectAccount, SubjectUserSid, MemberSid, MemberName, GroupName = TargetUserName
